00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:13,319
So I thought to spend them on the Buddha himself.

7
00:01:14,201 --> 00:01:25,525
And this particular discourse, number 67 at Chathuma, it's a place in the Sakyamuni country where he's from, shows us a little bit of tough love.

8
00:01:26,186 --> 00:01:30,956
So he wasn't always a huggy-wuggy, touchy-feely sort of person.

9
00:01:33,939 --> 00:01:48,498
So he was living at Chatumar and on that occasion, 500 monks headed by Venerable Sariputra and Venerable Moggallana, they were his two lieutenants, came to see the Blessed One.

10
00:01:49,379 --> 00:02:02,057
And while visiting those monks, exchanging greetings with the resident monks and were preparing resting places and putting away their bowls and outer robes, they were very loud and noisy.

11
00:02:03,099 --> 00:02:06,944
So the Blessed One said to Ananda, who are these noisy people?

12
00:02:07,045 --> 00:02:10,068
It's almost like fishermen hauling fish.

13
00:02:11,009 --> 00:02:13,293
He's got hawking fish, but I think it should be hauling fish.

14
00:02:14,715 --> 00:02:20,162
So Ananda said to him, well, it's these 500 bhikkhus that have come with Sariputra and Moggallana.

15
00:02:20,481 --> 00:02:27,830
So he said, right, in my name, go and tell those monks to come and see me, in so many words.

16
00:02:28,271 --> 00:02:29,152
Yes, Venerable Sir.

17
00:02:30,414 --> 00:02:32,296
So off...

18
00:02:32,445 --> 00:02:44,239
Off they went and these 500 monks turned up and they went to the Blessed One paying homage to him, sat to one side and the Blessed One said, Bhikkhus, why are you so loud and noisy?

19
00:02:44,459 --> 00:02:46,781
One should think you're fishermen hauling fish.

20
00:02:48,423 --> 00:02:56,951
And they said, well, we're part of the 500 Bhikkhus headed by Sariputta Moggallana who've come to see you, oh Blessed One.

21
00:02:58,062 --> 00:03:02,508
And while we were visiting, of course, we were being greeted by resident monks.

22
00:03:03,849 --> 00:03:08,496
And the Buddha said, fine, he said, go, because I dismiss you.

23
00:03:08,876 --> 00:03:10,117
You cannot live with me.

24
00:03:10,397 --> 00:03:11,419
That's a bit sharp, isn't it?

25
00:03:11,979 --> 00:03:16,826
I mean, they've come a long way to see him and they made a bit of a noise and he's chucked them out.

26
00:03:19,370 --> 00:03:21,793
Yes, venerable sir, they said very meekly, I suppose.

27
00:03:22,394 --> 00:03:24,597
And they rose, paid homage and off they went.

28
00:03:24,616 --> 00:03:27,039
They had to get all their stuff and move out.

29
00:03:28,555 --> 00:03:35,742
Now, on that occasion, the Sakyams of Chatuma had met together in the assembly hall for some business or other.

30
00:03:36,644 --> 00:03:41,449
And seeing the monks coming in a distance, they went to them and asked, what's going on?

31
00:03:42,671 --> 00:03:45,895
Friends, the Sangha of Bhikkhus has been dismissed by the Blessed One.

32
00:03:46,156 --> 00:03:47,176
He sent us away.

33
00:03:49,118 --> 00:03:55,186
Or then they said, well, look, stay here, be seated, and we will go and restore his confidence.

34
00:03:56,146 --> 00:03:58,409
So these very good Sakyams...

35
00:03:58,643 --> 00:04:08,474
who were obviously of the same group as the Buddha, his tribe, whatever you want to call it, went to see him.

36
00:04:08,875 --> 00:04:18,567
And they said, blessed one, let the blessed one delight in the sangha of monks.

37
00:04:19,708 --> 00:04:21,250
Welcome the sangha of monks.

38
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:26,136
Show compassion towards the sangha.

39
00:04:27,077 --> 00:04:50,401
as he used to show compassion towards it in the past these are new because just gone forth recently come to the dharma and discipline if they can get no opportunities to see the blessed one they may take place that there may take place in him some change or alteration which means for the worse of course they might they might give up they might go to another teacher

40
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:57,266
Just as when young seedlings get no water, they may take place in them some change or alteration.

41
00:04:58,146 --> 00:05:06,995
Just as when a young calf does not see its mother, there may take in it some change or alteration.

42
00:05:11,841 --> 00:05:18,668
So they're telling the Buddha to please forgive the bhikkhus, get them back just in case they go off.

43
00:05:19,271 --> 00:05:26,439
Now at the same time, Brahma Sahampati, he's the God who turned up when the Buddha was fully liberated.

44
00:05:27,321 --> 00:05:35,089
And when he sat there wondering whether he should tell anybody about this or not, wondering whether anybody would actually understand what he had to teach.

45
00:05:35,690 --> 00:05:41,817
And it was this Brahma, this great God who came down and said, well, there are some who got a little dust in their eyes.

46
00:05:42,478 --> 00:05:45,802
And that's when he thought about his past teachers,

47
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:55,050
And then he thought about the five companions whom he'd left and his teachings began on the prompting of Brahma Sahampati.

48
00:05:55,232 --> 00:06:00,961
So this was such an occasion that the Brahma thought that he ought to go down and have a chat.

49
00:06:02,101 --> 00:06:05,767
So he appeared before the Buddha.

50
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:11,858
And of course, he says exactly the same thing as the Sakyams did.

51
00:06:12,985 --> 00:06:22,817
The Sakhyams of Chattuma and Brahma Sampati were able to restore the Buddha's confidence with the similes of the seedlings and the young calf.

52
00:06:24,538 --> 00:06:29,165
So Moggallana said, get up, friends, take your bowls and outer robes.

53
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:33,651
The Blessed One's confidence has been restored and we're going back to see him.

54
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:35,091
So off they went.

55
00:06:35,612 --> 00:06:42,942
And when they've done so, when they're paying respects, the Buddha said to

56
00:06:43,225 --> 00:06:45,307
Venerable Sariputta.

57
00:06:46,048 --> 00:06:50,113
What did you think, Sariputta, when the Sangha of Bhikkhus was dismissed by me?

58
00:06:50,514 --> 00:06:51,175
What did you do?

59
00:06:52,677 --> 00:06:53,959
Venerable Sir, I thought thus.

60
00:06:54,038 --> 00:06:56,901
The Sangha of Bhikkhus has been dismissed by the Blessed One.

61
00:06:57,903 --> 00:07:03,329
The Blessed One will now abide inactive, devoted to pleasant abiding here and now.

62
00:07:04,531 --> 00:07:10,358
And we too shall now abide inactive, devoted to pleasant abiding here and now.

63
00:07:10,418 --> 00:07:11,781
In other words, meditation.

64
00:07:12,233 --> 00:07:14,115
Stop, Sariputta, stop.

65
00:07:14,134 --> 00:07:15,956
No, no, no, don't think that way.

66
00:07:15,997 --> 00:07:18,600
Such a thought should not be entertained by you again.

67
00:07:19,761 --> 00:07:24,545
And then he turned to Moggallana and said, what did you think, Moggallana?

68
00:07:24,565 --> 00:07:27,529
And Moggallana said, venerable sir, I thought this way.

69
00:07:27,889 --> 00:07:30,992
The Sangha Bhikkhus has been dismissed by the Blessed One.

70
00:07:31,713 --> 00:07:36,939
The Blessed One will now abide inactive, devoted to the pleasant abiding here and now.

71
00:07:37,841 --> 00:07:39,742
Now, venerable Sariputta and I,

72
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:43,045
shall lead the Sangha of Bhikkhus.

73
00:07:43,064 --> 00:07:46,170
Good, good, well said, Moggallana.

74
00:07:46,812 --> 00:07:52,601
Either I shall lead the Sangha or else Sariputta and Moggallana shall lead it.

75
00:07:52,622 --> 00:08:02,439
So here we see that the Buddha had in mind that these two younger persons than him, I think they would have been maybe 10 or so years younger,

76
00:08:03,802 --> 00:08:07,447
would have led the Sangha after he died.

77
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:09,649
But unfortunately, they both died before him.

78
00:08:10,410 --> 00:08:11,891
Sariputta died at home.

79
00:08:11,951 --> 00:08:13,434
He went back to see his family.

80
00:08:13,853 --> 00:08:24,125
And Moggallana, it seems, was attacked and murdered by another set of ascetics because he was converting their people, which is a bit sad, isn't it?

